<!-- @after Common Misconceptions :: check -->
**Which tool?** Decide before opening each answer.

<details><summary>Count analytics events from many coroutines.</summary>

`AtomicLong.incrementAndGet()`, or `MutableStateFlow.update { it + 1 }`: one atomic operation, no lock.
</details>

<details><summary>Refresh a token once when several requests see it expire at the same time.</summary>

`Mutex.withLock`: re-check the token inside the lock so only the first caller refreshes and the rest reuse its result.
</details>

<details><summary>A large in-memory cache updated thousands of times a second.</summary>

Confine it: one single-threaded dispatcher or actor owns the cache, and callers send it requests. No lock per access.
</details>
